1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,800
Welcome, detective! Let us use numbers to prepare our school
fair.

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:11,358
Two hundreds, three tens, and six ones make two hundred
thirty-six.

3
00:00:11,578 --> 00:00:13,577
It is greater than two hundred thirty.

4
00:00:13,797 --> 00:00:20,500
Compare the place values, starting with the hundreds.

5
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,449
Addition joins amounts.

6
00:00:23,605 --> 00:00:26,265
Twenty-seven plus fifteen is forty-two.

7
00:00:26,378 --> 00:00:29,102
Exchange ten ones for one ten when needed.

8
00:00:29,322 --> 00:00:31,492
Subtraction takes an amount away.

9
00:00:31,669 --> 00:00:34,585
Forty-two minus fifteen returns us to twenty-seven.

10
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:42,500
The operations help check each other.

11
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:46,842
Three bags with five pencils each make fifteen pencils.

12
00:00:47,041 --> 00:00:49,552
That is multiplication: equal groups.

13
00:00:49,814 --> 00:00:52,816
Sharing fifteen equally among three bags gives five each.

14
00:00:52,972 --> 00:00:53,904
That is division.

15
00:00:54,081 --> 00:01:02,500
Check that every bag has the same number.

16
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:05,325
Multiples follow equal jumps.

17
00:01:05,484 --> 00:01:07,184
Count in threes or fives.

18
00:01:07,404 --> 00:01:15,500
Fifteen appears in both patterns, so one number can fit two
rules.

19
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:18,804
Fractions describe equal parts of a whole.

20
00:01:19,002 --> 00:01:20,958
One of four parts is one quarter.

21
00:01:21,221 --> 00:01:22,878
Two quarters make one half.

22
00:01:23,141 --> 00:01:29,500
Three shaded parts make three quarters.

23
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:34,038
Three thousand plus four thousand costs seven thousand rupiah.

24
00:01:34,098 --> 00:01:35,158
Pay ten thousand.

25
00:01:35,378 --> 00:01:40,398
How much change?

26
00:01:40,588 --> 00:01:48,300
Three thousand: subtract the cost from your payment.

27
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,239
Read, choose your method, and check your answer.

28
00:01:55,416 --> 00:01:59,800
Try the Unit One quizzes!
